WEBVTT

00:09.010 --> 00:12.013
♪ I'm going down to South Park,
gonna have myself a time ♪

00:12.138 --> 00:13.889
♪ Friendly faces everywhere ♪

00:14.015 --> 00:16.017
♪ Humble folks
without temptation ♪

00:16.142 --> 00:18.728
♪ Going down to South Park,
gonna leave my woes behind ♪

00:18.853 --> 00:20.646
♪ Ample parking day or night ♪

00:20.771 --> 00:22.648
♪ People spouting,
"howdy, neighbor" ♪

00:22.773 --> 00:25.067
♪ Heading on up to South Park,
gonna see if I can't unwind ♪

00:25.192 --> 00:29.196
♪ Mrph rmhmhm rm!
Mrph rmhmhm rm! ♪

00:29.321 --> 00:31.824
♪ Come on down to South Park
and meet some friends of mine ♪

00:34.994 --> 00:37.913
Okay, children, we have
a special guest today --

00:38.039 --> 00:41.000
a woman recruiting young people
for a national choir tour.

00:41.125 --> 00:43.711
Now, I know that choir tours
are totally stupid and lame,

00:43.836 --> 00:45.921
but please give her
your full attention.

00:46.047 --> 00:47.298
Go ahead.

00:47.423 --> 00:48.841
Uh, thank you,
Mr. Garrison.

00:48.966 --> 00:50.843
How are we all doing
today?

00:52.344 --> 00:53.721
I can't hear you!

00:53.846 --> 00:55.139
I said,
"how are we all doing?"

00:55.264 --> 00:57.099
[farts]

00:57.224 --> 00:58.768
Eric Cartman,
you say "excuse me"!

00:58.893 --> 01:00.269
Okay.

01:00.394 --> 01:01.520
Go ahead.

01:01.645 --> 01:02.938
Children, we are
a national choir called

01:03.064 --> 01:04.774
"Getting Gay With Kids."

01:04.899 --> 01:06.650
We're gonna do a big tour
down in Central America

01:06.776 --> 01:10.029
to help save the rainforest,
and you can be a part of it.

01:10.154 --> 01:12.740
Mrph rmhmhm rm.
- [laughter]

01:12.865 --> 01:14.700
Kenny McCormick, you speak
when you're spoken to!

01:15.826 --> 01:17.328
Go ahead.

01:17.453 --> 01:18.871
You see, we take kids
from all over the country

01:18.996 --> 01:19.872
and put them in a choir
where we sing and dance

01:19.997 --> 01:21.457
[yawns]

01:21.582 --> 01:24.168
to raise awareness about
our vanishing rainforests.

01:24.293 --> 01:26.170
Did you know over
10,000 acres of rainforest

01:26.295 --> 01:27.922
are bulldozed every year?

01:28.047 --> 01:30.341
That's right, and over
30% of the world's oxygen

01:30.466 --> 01:31.842
is made
in the rainforest.

01:31.967 --> 01:34.804
Miss Stevens: So,
who wants to join the fun?

01:34.929 --> 01:35.930
What if you don't
have any rhythm?

01:36.055 --> 01:37.807
Excuse me?
- Like my friend Kyle.

01:37.932 --> 01:39.100
He's Jewish so
he doesn't have any rhythm.

01:39.225 --> 01:40.559
Shut up, fat-ass!
- Choirs suck.

01:40.684 --> 01:42.394
Kyle Broflovski,
you watch your language!

01:42.520 --> 01:44.063
Eric Cartman,
you be nice to people!

01:44.188 --> 01:45.815
Stan Marsh,
you mind your manners!

01:45.940 --> 01:47.316
Kenny McCormick,
you pay attention!

01:47.441 --> 01:49.110
[exhales] Go ahead.

01:49.235 --> 01:50.528
Well, that's all,
really.

01:50.653 --> 01:52.321
So if anyone is interested

01:52.446 --> 01:53.697
in seeing the rainforest
and joining our choir,

01:53.823 --> 01:56.075
I'll leave information packets
up front.

01:56.200 --> 01:57.284
That's good. We need
some more toilet paper.

01:57.409 --> 01:58.494
[laughter]

01:58.619 --> 02:00.121
Alright,
that does it!

02:00.246 --> 02:02.665
Mr. Mackey: I am tired
of seeing you in my office.

02:02.790 --> 02:05.251
You get sent here
every day, Craig.

02:05.376 --> 02:06.377
I know.

02:06.502 --> 02:07.711
Why can't you behave?

02:07.837 --> 02:09.296
I don't know.

02:09.421 --> 02:10.840
What do you have to say
for yourself?

02:10.965 --> 02:14.093
Well, I'll tell you what,
young man,

02:14.218 --> 02:16.387
you're gonna be held back
a grade if you don't--

02:16.512 --> 02:18.514
Did you just flip me off?!
- No.

02:18.639 --> 02:20.307
Yes, you did.
You just flipped me the bird.

02:20.432 --> 02:23.018
Now, see, this is exactly
what I'm talking about.

02:23.144 --> 02:25.312
If you don't shape up, m'kay,
and get your head straight--

02:25.437 --> 02:26.772
There! You just
flipped me off again!

02:26.897 --> 02:28.274
No, I didn't.
- Yes, you did!

02:28.399 --> 02:30.192
And until you stop
flipping people off,

02:30.317 --> 02:31.819
you can just go back
to the waiting room, m'kay?

02:31.944 --> 02:32.945
Next!

02:33.070 --> 02:34.989
Well, well, well,

02:35.114 --> 02:37.032
if it isn't Stan, Kyle,
Kenny, and Eric.

02:37.158 --> 02:38.534
Hey, Craig.
- Hey, don't flip me off,

02:38.659 --> 02:39.326
you son of a bitch!

02:39.451 --> 02:41.412
Sit down, boys.

02:41.537 --> 02:43.581
Let's see, what did Mr. Garrison
send <i>you</i> in here for?

02:43.706 --> 02:46.041
"The boys were being rude
while a choir teacher

02:46.167 --> 02:47.918
was giving
some stupid presentation."

02:48.043 --> 02:49.837
It's just some dumb
activist kids' choir thing.

02:49.962 --> 02:51.589
Young man,
"Getting Gay With Kids"

02:51.714 --> 02:53.549
is not dumb, m'kay?

02:53.674 --> 02:55.467
It just so happens that
I'm on the board of directors.

02:55.593 --> 02:57.469
Dude, all those choirs
are the same.

02:57.595 --> 02:59.180
They don't even really sing.
They use prerecorded tapes.

02:59.305 --> 03:01.182
Well, guess what, boys?

03:01.307 --> 03:02.850
I think "Getting Gay With Kids"
is just what you need.

03:02.975 --> 03:04.560
I'm gonna sign up
all four of you.

03:04.685 --> 03:05.936
What?!
- You can't do that!

03:06.061 --> 03:07.354
Mrph rm!

03:07.479 --> 03:09.064
Mrph rm, mrph.

03:09.190 --> 03:11.150
I think this will be
very good for you.

03:11.275 --> 03:12.776
But we don't even care
about the rainforest.

03:12.902 --> 03:15.446
And that's exactly
why you need to go, m'kay?

03:15.571 --> 03:16.989
Please, Mr. Mackey,
we'll be good!

03:17.114 --> 03:18.782
Don't send us
to that old kids' choir!

03:18.908 --> 03:20.576
Have mercy, Mr. Mackey!

03:21.660 --> 03:23.329
Be safe, Kyle.

03:23.454 --> 03:24.788
Bring me something back
from the rainforest.

03:24.914 --> 03:27.333
Oh, no, the rainforest
is very fragile.

03:27.458 --> 03:30.085
We must take only pictures
and leave only footprints.

03:30.211 --> 03:31.462
Oh,
I didn't realize.

03:31.587 --> 03:33.130
Did you know
that right now,

03:33.255 --> 03:35.049
bulldozers are tearing down
thousand of acres

03:35.174 --> 03:36.634
of rainforest
every day?

03:36.759 --> 03:38.969
Ah, man, this is
gonna suck donkey balls.

03:39.094 --> 03:41.597
Please, don't make me go on
a choir tour, mom! Please!

03:41.722 --> 03:43.390
Stan,
you should be excited.

03:43.515 --> 03:45.226
I would love to see
the rainforest.

03:45.351 --> 03:46.936
Besides, your dad and I
need some time alone.

03:47.061 --> 03:48.437
Noooo!

03:51.941 --> 03:53.567
Okay, children,
that's all of us.

03:53.692 --> 03:55.819
We're ready to head for
the Latin-American nation

03:55.945 --> 03:57.363
of Costa Rica,

03:57.488 --> 03:59.698
a country filled
with virgin rainforest.

03:59.823 --> 04:01.700
Whoopee.

04:01.825 --> 04:04.453
And you must be Eric Cartman.
I've heard about you.

04:04.578 --> 04:06.789
You don't respect nature
or other cultures.

04:06.914 --> 04:08.374
Yeah, pretty much.

04:08.499 --> 04:10.626
Well, I'm gonna change
the way you think, kiddo.

04:10.751 --> 04:12.211
My name's Kelly.

04:12.336 --> 04:14.213
Mrph rm rmphm.
- Lenny?

04:14.338 --> 04:15.506
Mrph rmphm!
- Johnny?

04:15.631 --> 04:17.132
Rmphm!
- Oh.

04:17.258 --> 04:18.884
Now, we've got a long trip
ahead of us,

04:19.009 --> 04:21.679
so let's take the opportunity
to learn our choreography.

04:21.804 --> 04:23.264
The nightmare begins.

04:23.389 --> 04:25.933
[Latin-American music plays]

04:32.564 --> 04:33.857
Oh, look, children!

04:33.983 --> 04:35.276
I think
we're entering San José,

04:35.401 --> 04:37.486
which is the capital
of Costa Rica.

04:37.611 --> 04:39.154
Oh, this is so exciting!

04:39.280 --> 04:41.198
Oh, my God, dude!

04:41.323 --> 04:42.866
Look how dirty
and crappy everything is!

04:42.992 --> 04:45.411
Eric, Costa Rica
is a third-world country.

04:45.536 --> 04:48.414
These people are much poorer
than those in the U.S.

04:48.539 --> 04:50.457
Why the hell
don't they get jobs?

04:50.582 --> 04:53.294
Hey! Why don't you people quit
slacking off and get a job?!

04:53.419 --> 04:55.004
What's wrong with you?!
Go to college!

04:55.129 --> 04:56.588
Eric, sit down!

04:56.714 --> 04:58.465
You gotta be firm
with these people

04:58.590 --> 05:00.384
or they just slack off and
be poor forever, right, Kenny?

05:00.509 --> 05:02.970
Hey, maybe that's it, Kenny.
Maybe you're Costa Rican.

05:03.095 --> 05:04.847
That's why your family's
so poor.

05:04.972 --> 05:07.057
Mrph rmhmhm rm.
- Your family <i>isn't</i> poor?

05:07.182 --> 05:09.018
Wow, dude,
look over there!

05:09.143 --> 05:11.312
Wow!
Costa Rican prostitutes!

05:11.437 --> 05:12.896
Hey, look at the prostitutes,
you guys!

05:16.150 --> 05:17.651
[Latin accent]
What are you looking at, man?

05:17.776 --> 05:20.195
[Latin accent] Yeah,
why don't you take a picture?

05:20.321 --> 05:22.197
Okay. Cleek!

05:22.323 --> 05:23.991
Miss Stevens:
Eric, sit down!

05:25.743 --> 05:27.995
Kids, this is the Costa Rican
Capitol building.

05:28.120 --> 05:29.747
This is where
all the leaders

05:29.872 --> 05:31.415
of the Costa Rican government
make their--

05:31.540 --> 05:33.125
Oh, my God, it smells
like ass out here!

05:33.250 --> 05:35.002
Alright,
that does it!

05:35.127 --> 05:36.795
Eric Cartman, you respect
other cultures this instant!

05:36.920 --> 05:38.714
I wasn't saying anything
about their culture.

05:38.839 --> 05:40.507
I'm just saying
their city smells like ass.

05:40.632 --> 05:42.426
Wow, seeing a place
like this

05:42.551 --> 05:44.303
really makes you appreciate
living in America, huh?

05:44.428 --> 05:45.929
Mrph rm.

05:46.055 --> 05:46.889
You may think
that making fun

05:47.014 --> 05:47.890
of third-world countries
is funny,

05:48.015 --> 05:48.932
but let me--

05:49.058 --> 05:50.267
I don't think
it's funny.

05:50.392 --> 05:51.477
This place is overcrowded,
smelly, and poor.

05:51.602 --> 05:53.562
That's not funny.
That sucks.

05:53.687 --> 05:55.439
Eric, will you please, <i>please,
just keep your mouth shut</i>

05:55.564 --> 05:57.358
while we present ourselves
to the Costa-Rican president?

05:57.483 --> 05:59.193
Why?

05:59.318 --> 06:00.069
Because I'll buy you
some ice cream if you do.

06:00.194 --> 06:01.195
[laughing] Oh!

06:01.320 --> 06:02.863
Well, it was a long trip,

06:02.988 --> 06:04.865
but the children are very
excited to sing tomorrow.

06:06.367 --> 06:07.493
<i>¿Qué?</i>

06:07.618 --> 06:09.244
Uh, we're the choir

06:09.370 --> 06:11.413
that-that was sent
from the United States.

06:12.498 --> 06:13.749
<i>¿Qué?</i>

06:13.874 --> 06:15.209
We're the group singing

06:15.334 --> 06:18.128
for the "Save the Rainforest"
summit tomorrow?

06:19.630 --> 06:20.923
Oh, dear,
where's Mr. Mackey?

06:21.048 --> 06:22.257
He should've been here
by now.

06:22.383 --> 06:23.509
Children, do any of you
speak Spanish?

06:23.634 --> 06:25.177
Don't you dare!

06:25.302 --> 06:27.179
Sorry I'm late.

06:27.304 --> 06:28.722
Oh, thank goodness you're here.
I don't speak any Spanish.

06:28.847 --> 06:30.432
Oh, no problem.

06:30.557 --> 06:33.102
<i>Usted es choir
de estados unidos, muy bien.</i>

06:33.227 --> 06:34.978
Oh, oh--
"Save the Rainforest."

06:35.104 --> 06:36.105
Yes!

06:36.230 --> 06:38.065
[speaking Spanish]

06:38.190 --> 06:41.318
He says, "Pablo here will take
you on a rainforest tour."

06:41.443 --> 06:42.361
Oh, boy!

06:42.486 --> 06:43.821
Mr. Presidente,

06:43.946 --> 06:44.947
round up
your subjects outside.

06:45.072 --> 06:46.740
We have a special gift
for you--

06:46.865 --> 06:49.159
The gift... of song.

06:49.910 --> 06:50.953
<i>¿Qué?</i>

06:51.078 --> 06:52.663
Alright, children,

06:52.788 --> 06:54.873
let's get in our rows quickly
so we can begin.

06:54.998 --> 06:56.708
Did you remember all
the choreography, Lenny?

06:56.834 --> 06:57.709
Mrph rmhmhm rm.

06:57.835 --> 06:59.420
Hello, everybody!

06:59.545 --> 07:01.046
This is just
a little rehearsal for tomorrow,

07:01.171 --> 07:02.714
so we may be
a little rusty.

07:02.840 --> 07:03.966
[chuckling]

07:04.091 --> 07:06.301
♪ Doo-doo-dee-doo ♪

07:06.427 --> 07:08.053
♪ Zada-doo-dee-wow ♪

07:08.178 --> 07:09.596
Boys: ♪ There's a place
that is magical ♪

07:09.721 --> 07:11.723
♪ And full of rain ♪

07:11.849 --> 07:14.601
Girls: ♪ But now it needs help
because it is in pain ♪

07:14.726 --> 07:17.813
All: ♪ Cleaning the earth
is a mighty big chore ♪

07:17.938 --> 07:23.026
♪ We're spreading awareness
like never before ♪

07:23.152 --> 07:26.071
♪ Getting Gay With Kids
is here ♪

07:26.196 --> 07:29.116
♪ To spread the word
and bring you cheer ♪

07:29.241 --> 07:32.744
♪ Let's save the rainforest,
what do you say? ♪

07:32.870 --> 07:36.290
♪ Being an activist
is totally gay ♪

07:36.415 --> 07:40.878
♪ And someday, if we work hard,
boys and girls ♪

07:41.003 --> 07:44.798
♪ There'll be nothing
but rainforest ♪

07:44.923 --> 07:47.092
♪ Covering
the entire world ♪

07:47.217 --> 07:48.177
♪ World! ♪

07:48.302 --> 07:49.720
♪ World! ♪

07:49.845 --> 07:52.514
♪ Getting Gay With Kids
is here ♪

07:52.639 --> 07:56.226
♪ To spread the word
and bring you cheer ♪

07:56.351 --> 07:58.979
♪ Getting Gay With Kids
is here ♪

07:59.104 --> 08:00.898
♪ So save the rainforest ♪

08:01.023 --> 08:02.608
♪ Totally gay ♪

08:02.733 --> 08:04.526
♪ It's totally gay! ♪

08:04.651 --> 08:06.195
[boom box clicks off]

08:07.696 --> 08:09.406
Great job, gang!

08:09.531 --> 08:10.616
You were really
all over the place, Kyle.

08:10.741 --> 08:12.075
Thanks.

08:12.201 --> 08:12.701
I told you Jewish people
don't have rhythm.

08:12.826 --> 08:14.328
Fuck off, Cartman!

08:14.453 --> 08:16.371
No, dude, I think Cartman
might actually be right.

08:16.497 --> 08:18.624
No!
That's a stereotype!

08:18.749 --> 08:21.126
Dude, maybe you really
don't have any rhythm.

08:26.048 --> 08:28.509
This is now secondary
rainforest we're entering.

08:28.634 --> 08:30.594
Notice the canopy
of foliage.

08:30.719 --> 08:33.347
Oh, it's everything
I ever dreamed it would be!

08:33.472 --> 08:34.348
Damn,
it's hot out here.

08:34.473 --> 08:35.724
Aah! Snake!

08:35.849 --> 08:36.850
No, dude,
that's a branch.

08:36.975 --> 08:38.810
Oh. Aah! Snake!

08:38.936 --> 08:39.978
No, that's
the same branch again.

08:40.103 --> 08:41.355
Oh.

08:41.480 --> 08:42.731
The rainforest
is very delicate,

08:42.856 --> 08:44.942
and we must take steps
to protect it.

08:45.067 --> 08:46.360
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

08:46.485 --> 08:47.778
Take steps,
blah, blah, blah.

08:47.903 --> 08:50.447
We hear this a million times
back up in the States.

08:50.572 --> 08:52.658
Here, look--
these are squirrel monkeys,

08:52.783 --> 08:55.327
endangered inhabitants
of the rainforest.

08:55.452 --> 08:56.912
Wow, isn't he neat,
Lenny?

08:57.037 --> 08:58.413
Bad! Bad monkey!

08:58.539 --> 08:59.998
Eric, what the heck
are you doing?!

09:00.123 --> 09:01.542
I'm asserting myself.

09:01.667 --> 09:03.377
It's tough love,
just like my Mr. Kitty.

09:03.502 --> 09:05.379
When he's bad, I say,
"that's a bad Mr. Kitty!"

09:05.504 --> 09:06.922
And I smack him
on the head!

09:07.047 --> 09:09.591
And here is
a three-toed sloth.

09:09.716 --> 09:11.593
It's bad--
that's a bad three-toed sloth!

09:11.718 --> 09:13.136
Eric, for God's sake,
knock it off!

09:13.262 --> 09:15.347
Respect my authoritah!

09:15.472 --> 09:16.932
Well, Mr. Pedro,
this was a great tour,

09:17.057 --> 09:18.767
but I guess we should be
heading back.

09:18.892 --> 09:20.435
We have a big concert tomorrow,
don't we, kids?

09:20.561 --> 09:22.020
Yeah!
Yeah!

09:22.145 --> 09:23.897
I wish we could've seen
the yanogapa.

09:24.022 --> 09:25.566
What's the Yanogapa?

09:25.691 --> 09:26.441
The Yanogapa
are a gentle native people

09:26.567 --> 09:28.193
that live
in the rainforest,

09:28.318 --> 09:30.279
but bulldozers
are destroying their homes.

09:30.404 --> 09:32.114
Soon, they will have
nowhere to go.

09:32.239 --> 09:34.241
So we must stop
bulldozing the rainforest --

09:34.366 --> 09:36.451
Oh, God,
here she goes again!

09:36.577 --> 09:38.078
Aah!
- Stanley, what is it?

09:38.203 --> 09:39.121
Snake!

09:39.246 --> 09:40.872
[all gasping]

09:40.998 --> 09:42.708
Oh, yes, this is what
we call a coral snake.

09:42.833 --> 09:44.668
Notice the red markings.
Quite an amazing creature.

09:44.793 --> 09:46.461
Aah!

09:46.587 --> 09:47.379
What's the matter,
little boy?

09:47.504 --> 09:48.630
He's a little wuss.
What's it look like?

09:48.755 --> 09:49.881
I'm just scared
of snakes.

09:50.007 --> 09:51.717
No, no,
you must remember,

09:51.842 --> 09:53.802
this snake is more afraid of us
than we are of it.

09:53.927 --> 09:55.345
Aah!

09:56.430 --> 09:57.806
[groans]

09:57.931 --> 09:59.224
Oh, my God!

10:00.976 --> 10:02.894
Yeah, that snake is really
scared of us, alright.

10:04.479 --> 10:06.732
Jesus Christ!
Is he dead?

10:06.857 --> 10:07.983
Dude!

10:08.108 --> 10:09.234
My guess
would be "yes."

10:09.359 --> 10:10.485
Oh, no! God, no!

10:10.611 --> 10:11.695
Now, don't panic, children.

10:11.820 --> 10:13.363
Bad!

10:13.488 --> 10:15.157
That's a bad snake--
aah!

10:17.868 --> 10:20.370
Maybe we came from that way.
No... No.

10:20.495 --> 10:21.872
Let's try this way.

10:21.997 --> 10:23.790
Lenny, do you think
we're gonna be okay?

10:23.915 --> 10:25.250
Mrph rmhmhm rm.

10:25.375 --> 10:27.252
That's good.
Can I tell you something?

10:27.377 --> 10:28.003
Mrph rm.
- I think I like you.

10:28.128 --> 10:29.588
Mrph?!

10:29.713 --> 10:31.965
Yeah, I think we
communicate really well.

10:32.090 --> 10:33.759
Mrph rmhmhm rm!
- No, that's not good.

10:33.884 --> 10:35.093
Mrph rmh rmphm?

10:35.218 --> 10:36.637
No. See, if I start to
like you too much,

10:36.762 --> 10:38.430
I'm only going to
get my heart broken,

10:38.555 --> 10:40.182
'cause we live on opposite ends
of the country.

10:40.307 --> 10:41.516
Once this choir tour
is over,

10:41.642 --> 10:42.684
we'll never see
each other again,

10:42.809 --> 10:44.311
and that would
devastate me!

10:44.436 --> 10:45.395
So I can't have
any feelings for you!

10:45.520 --> 10:48.106
I just can't, Lenny!
- Mrph!

10:48.231 --> 10:49.858
Oh, children,
the sun is setting.

10:49.983 --> 10:51.401
We have to find our way
out of here, quick!

10:54.696 --> 10:57.699
[thunder crashes]

10:57.824 --> 10:59.117
Okay, okay.

10:59.242 --> 11:01.328
Everything is just fine,
kids.

11:01.453 --> 11:03.914
Now, it is important
that we all stick together.

11:04.039 --> 11:06.124
Is everybody still here?

11:06.249 --> 11:07.209
Boy: I'm not.

11:07.334 --> 11:08.585
Who's not?

11:08.710 --> 11:10.045
Me.

11:10.170 --> 11:12.881
Lenny, will you
hold my hand?

11:13.006 --> 11:15.342
I don't want to get
emotionally attached, though.

11:15.467 --> 11:17.469
Oh, my God, dude!
I just saw Tony Danza!

11:17.594 --> 11:20.180
No, you didn't just see
Tony Danza, Stanley.

11:22.099 --> 11:25.060
[rooster crowing]

11:26.687 --> 11:27.646
<i>Bueno. Bueno.</i>

11:27.771 --> 11:29.940
[speaking Spanish]

11:30.065 --> 11:32.234
[speaking Spanish]

12:01.430 --> 12:02.848
Stan: Dude,
we're totally lost.

12:02.973 --> 12:04.474
We're gonna die out here.
- Kelly: We are?

12:04.599 --> 12:06.226
Don't worry, Kelly,

12:06.351 --> 12:07.477
we're gonna find our way
out of the rainforest

12:07.602 --> 12:08.979
and make it back
to the concert in time.

12:09.104 --> 12:11.189
We just need to respect
our mother rainforest,

12:11.314 --> 12:13.233
and she will respect us.

12:13.358 --> 12:14.985
Mrs. Stevens, you have
a bug on your back.

12:15.110 --> 12:16.445
Oh, really?
Could you brush it off?

12:16.570 --> 12:17.988
[roaring]

12:18.113 --> 12:19.656
Um, no.

12:19.781 --> 12:21.992
Whoa! Oh, my God!
Get it off me!

12:22.117 --> 12:24.327
For the love of God,
get it off me!

12:24.453 --> 12:26.371
Oh, my God!
[insect roaring]

12:26.496 --> 12:28.540
Okay, children,
we must understand

12:28.665 --> 12:30.834
that the insects
of the rainforest

12:30.959 --> 12:33.128
help the delicate balance
of life here.

12:33.253 --> 12:35.505
[roaring]
Oh, my God!

12:35.630 --> 12:36.631
The rainforest sucks.
I want to go home.

12:36.757 --> 12:37.799
Me too!

12:37.924 --> 12:39.968
[children grumbling]

12:40.093 --> 12:41.928
Shh, children.

12:42.053 --> 12:44.765
Let's try to listen to
what the rainforest tells us.

12:44.890 --> 12:46.349
And if we use our ears,

12:46.475 --> 12:48.518
she can tell us
so many things --

12:48.643 --> 12:49.936
Aah!
There's a dude here.

12:50.061 --> 12:51.897
Oh, thank goodness!
Hello, sir, we are lost.

12:52.022 --> 12:54.566
[chuckling]
Can you help us?

12:55.567 --> 12:56.818
<i>¿Qué?</i>

12:56.943 --> 12:58.320
Let me try, let me try.

12:58.445 --> 13:00.489
We are from America--
A-mer-ica.

13:00.614 --> 13:02.657
We are lost
and very hungry.

13:02.783 --> 13:04.743
<i>Necesito burritos.</i>

13:04.868 --> 13:06.495
I don't want a burrito,
I want a taco... supreme.

13:06.620 --> 13:08.079
A taco.

13:08.205 --> 13:09.122
I want two tostadas
with mild sauce.

13:09.247 --> 13:12.167
Two tostadas...

13:12.292 --> 13:14.377
Boys, not every Spanish person
eats tacos and burritos.

13:14.503 --> 13:15.962
That's a stereotype.

13:16.087 --> 13:18.632
Children, he wants us
to follow him.

13:18.757 --> 13:20.008
Oh, thank goodness!

13:20.133 --> 13:22.010
I think this ordeal
is over.

13:24.387 --> 13:26.139
This doesn't look
very safe.

13:26.264 --> 13:27.766
Yeah, I think we should
get the hell out of here.

13:27.891 --> 13:29.976
Now, kids, let's be
a bit more open-minded.

13:30.101 --> 13:31.728
I've read all about this
in <i>Newsweek.</i>

13:31.853 --> 13:33.271
This is a people's army.

13:33.396 --> 13:35.190
They are fighting
the fascist policies

13:35.315 --> 13:36.525
of their fascist government.

13:36.650 --> 13:38.151
Oh, hello.

13:38.276 --> 13:39.778
Do you speak, uh, English?

13:39.903 --> 13:41.571
Who are you?
- Oh, wonderful!

13:41.696 --> 13:43.573
We were lost, and it is
such a great coincidence

13:43.698 --> 13:45.534
we found you.

13:45.659 --> 13:47.118
We're here to protest
the government-sanctioned raping

13:47.244 --> 13:48.203
of your rainforest.

13:49.704 --> 13:51.122
We are fighters,
just like you.

13:51.248 --> 13:52.874
Could you help us
get back to San José?

13:52.999 --> 13:57.170
Um...oh, I know!
Perhaps you would like a gift.

13:57.295 --> 13:59.339
Well, we have only
one gift to give--

13:59.464 --> 14:01.424
the gift of song.

14:01.550 --> 14:02.592
[groaning]

14:02.717 --> 14:04.469
♪ Doo-doo-dee-doo ♪

14:04.594 --> 14:05.971
♪ Zada-doo-dee-wow ♪

14:06.096 --> 14:07.472
Boys: ♪ There's a place
that is magical ♪

14:07.597 --> 14:09.182
♪ And full of rain ♪

14:09.307 --> 14:12.435
Kyle, for the love of God,
do the right choreography.

14:12.561 --> 14:15.772
All: ♪ Cleaning the earth
is a mighty big chore ♪

14:15.897 --> 14:18.400
♪ We're spreading awareness
like never before ♪

14:18.525 --> 14:20.861
Oh, Kyle, please!

14:20.986 --> 14:23.446
♪ Getting Gay With Kids
is here ♪

14:23.572 --> 14:24.906
Enough!

14:25.031 --> 14:26.408
Well, we hope that
our gift of song

14:26.533 --> 14:28.118
has warmed your hearts.

14:28.243 --> 14:30.453
We're not getting gay
with any kids, okay?

14:30.579 --> 14:33.081
Uh, yeah, so... do you have
a phone we could use?

14:33.206 --> 14:35.000
Yes, we have a phone.

14:35.125 --> 14:37.419
It's right over there,
next to the 12-person jacuzzi.

14:37.544 --> 14:40.881
[laughter]

14:41.006 --> 14:43.008
Now, get out of here
before we kill you!

14:43.133 --> 14:44.968
If it's because of the little
Jewish boy's choreography--

14:45.093 --> 14:46.887
Hey!

14:47.012 --> 14:48.013
You whacked Americans
make me sick.

14:48.138 --> 14:50.098
You waste food, oil,
and everything else

14:50.223 --> 14:52.475
because you're so rich, and then
you tell the rest of the world

14:52.601 --> 14:53.977
to save the rainforest

14:54.102 --> 14:55.228
because you like
its pretty flowers.

14:55.353 --> 14:58.148
[gunfire]

14:58.273 --> 14:59.649
Aah!
Aah!

14:59.774 --> 15:00.817
<i>Rápido! Rápido!</i>

15:02.986 --> 15:04.154
Miss Stevens:
Run, children, run!

15:22.589 --> 15:25.050
Hello? Anybody?

15:25.175 --> 15:26.551
Help!

15:26.676 --> 15:28.053
Wow, look at
the pretty flower.

15:28.178 --> 15:29.679
Oh, no, no, no, Jake.

15:29.804 --> 15:31.806
That fragile flower
is very delicate.

15:31.932 --> 15:33.266
[muffled] Aah!
Ow, it hurts!

15:33.391 --> 15:35.393
Aah!

15:35.518 --> 15:38.271
[crying] I want to go home!
I hate the rainforest!

15:38.396 --> 15:39.648
Mrph rmhmhm rm.

15:39.773 --> 15:41.524
Oh, Lenny, hold me.

15:41.650 --> 15:43.777
No,
I can't get attached.

15:43.902 --> 15:45.904
But I do like you.
- Mrph rmh rmphm.

15:46.029 --> 15:47.155
But you're only
going to leave me.

15:47.280 --> 15:48.740
Mrph rmhmhm rm!

15:48.865 --> 15:50.325
We're here live
in San José, Costa Rica,

15:50.450 --> 15:52.452
where hundreds of
rich Americans have gathered

15:52.577 --> 15:54.371
for the "Save the
Rainforest" summit.

15:54.496 --> 15:56.331
Everyone is here so they can
feel good about themselves

15:56.456 --> 15:58.166
and act like they aren't
the ones responsible

15:58.291 --> 15:59.626
for the rainforest's
peril.

15:59.751 --> 16:01.419
That's right, Bob,
and, of course,

16:01.544 --> 16:03.421
the main attraction today
is the darling kids' choir

16:03.546 --> 16:05.131
"Getting Gay With Kids,"

16:05.256 --> 16:06.967
all of whom must be
backstage preparing

16:07.092 --> 16:08.259
at this very moment.

16:08.385 --> 16:09.844
[birds squawking]

16:09.970 --> 16:11.680
Oh, there's just
no end to this place.

16:11.805 --> 16:13.473
I think maybe
we're going in circles.

16:13.598 --> 16:15.183
Oh, dear God!
The summit starts in an hour.

16:15.308 --> 16:16.351
I'm going to lose my job.

16:16.476 --> 16:17.519
[roaring]
Aah!

16:17.644 --> 16:19.521
This is bull crap.

16:19.646 --> 16:20.730
I am not following this
stupid hippie around anymore.

16:20.855 --> 16:22.857
Where are you going?
- I'm going this way.

16:22.983 --> 16:24.651
Young man,
I am the adult here,

16:24.776 --> 16:26.111
and I say
you go <i>this</i> way!

16:26.236 --> 16:27.988
Look,
you can stay over nah,

16:28.113 --> 16:29.572
but I'm going over nah!

16:29.698 --> 16:31.408
Young man,
I have had it!

16:31.533 --> 16:33.952
No, no, no --
you nah, me nah.

16:34.077 --> 16:36.913
Screw you guys!
I'm going home.

16:37.038 --> 16:40.542
Good! You deserve to die,
you little bastard!

16:40.667 --> 16:42.460
Eric, we have to
stay together!

16:42.585 --> 16:43.962
God damn stupid
hippie activist.

16:44.087 --> 16:45.588
I should be home
nestled on the couch

16:45.714 --> 16:47.048
with my Mr. Kitty right now

16:47.173 --> 16:49.843
watching "Fat Albert"
cartoons...

16:49.968 --> 16:52.262
Yes! I knew it!
I'm saved!

16:52.387 --> 16:53.638
Hey, maybe Cartman
was right.

16:53.763 --> 16:55.390
Yeah, it happened
once before.

16:55.515 --> 16:58.768
No, the spirit of Maya
has told me to go <i>this</i> way.

16:58.893 --> 17:00.603
Mister, you gotta help me!
I'm starving to death.

17:00.729 --> 17:01.646
What are you doing here,
little boy?

17:01.771 --> 17:03.440
I was with my class,

17:03.565 --> 17:04.482
and we got lost rainforest,
and I need some food!

17:04.607 --> 17:05.984
I'm fading fast!

17:06.109 --> 17:07.027
Lost in the rainforest?
Oh, my Lord!

17:07.152 --> 17:08.361
Where are
all the others?

17:08.486 --> 17:10.572
Food!
I have to have food!

17:10.697 --> 17:13.825
Oh, my God! Get this child
some food, quick!

17:13.950 --> 17:15.201
Chicken wings.

17:15.326 --> 17:17.412
Chicken wings!
Medium spicy.

17:17.537 --> 17:21.249
Crowd: [chanting]
Start the show! Start the show!

17:41.603 --> 17:42.979
[laughing]

17:49.986 --> 17:51.237
Oh, God,
this is a nightmare!

17:51.362 --> 17:52.947
We're never going to
make the festival.

17:53.073 --> 17:54.532
Hey, look over there.
Isn't that smoke?

17:54.657 --> 17:57.744
Let's go, quickly!

17:57.869 --> 17:59.871
Hey, it's a fire. That means
there must be people.

17:59.996 --> 18:01.081
[rustling]

18:03.458 --> 18:05.293
Children,
it's the Yanogapa!

18:05.418 --> 18:07.003
Do not be afraid.

18:07.128 --> 18:09.672
We are not here to tear down
your rainforest.

18:09.798 --> 18:11.049
[speaking
native language]

18:11.174 --> 18:12.550
[speaking
native language]

18:12.675 --> 18:14.677
Look how they live in peace
with all living things.

18:14.803 --> 18:16.638
Gentle, noble...

18:16.763 --> 18:19.724
Run for your lives children!
- Holy crap!

18:19.849 --> 18:22.477
[yanogapa chanting
in native language]

18:22.602 --> 18:24.229
Jesus Christ!
- Run, run, run!

18:24.354 --> 18:25.897
[roaring]
Aah!

18:26.022 --> 18:27.982
Aah! Lenny!

18:32.320 --> 18:34.614
What the hell?
I'm sinking.

18:34.739 --> 18:35.740
It's quicksand!

18:35.865 --> 18:38.368
[chanting quickens]

18:46.292 --> 18:48.086
All we ever heard
growing up

18:48.211 --> 18:48.878
was "save the rainforest,"
"the rainforest is fragile."

18:49.003 --> 18:50.421
Yeah, fragile my ass!

18:50.547 --> 18:51.464
Larry, if we
make it out of this,

18:51.589 --> 18:53.007
I want to be
your girlfriend.

18:53.133 --> 18:54.259
Even if we do live
in different places,

18:54.384 --> 18:55.260
I don't care.

18:55.385 --> 18:57.637
Mrph rmhmhm rm.

18:57.762 --> 19:00.431
[Yanogapa chanting
in native language]

19:00.557 --> 19:04.561
Okay, just what the heck
is going on here, people?

19:04.686 --> 19:06.646
[chanting continues]

19:06.771 --> 19:10.608
[chanting slowly]

19:12.986 --> 19:14.028
Aaaah!

19:14.154 --> 19:16.030
Oh, no!

19:16.156 --> 19:17.198
That big thing is going to
make love to Miss Stevens!

19:17.323 --> 19:19.242
Alright, that does it!

19:19.367 --> 19:21.369
God damn,
stupid-ass rainforest!

19:21.494 --> 19:23.913
This place fucking sucks!

19:24.038 --> 19:24.998
I was wrong!
Fuck the rainforest!

19:25.123 --> 19:26.082
I fucking hate it!

19:26.207 --> 19:27.458
I fucking hate it!

19:27.584 --> 19:29.127
<i>Now</i> she figures it out.

19:29.252 --> 19:31.796
Quick!
Everybody help the children!

19:33.381 --> 19:35.133
Hyah!

19:35.258 --> 19:37.218
[chanting]

19:42.056 --> 19:44.017
Wow!
Dude, bulldozers rule!

19:44.142 --> 19:45.518
Come on, let's get you
back to civilization!

19:45.643 --> 19:46.686
All: Hooray!

19:46.811 --> 19:48.605
Hooray, children!

19:48.730 --> 19:50.064
How did you know
where we were?

19:50.190 --> 19:51.024
Your little friend
helped me out.

19:51.149 --> 19:52.442
Eric?

19:52.567 --> 19:53.693
Who'd you expect?
Merv Griffin?

19:53.818 --> 19:55.486
What exactly are you guys
doing out here

19:55.612 --> 19:57.322
with all this
construction equipment?

19:57.447 --> 19:59.365
We're clearing out
big sections of the rainforest

19:59.490 --> 20:00.617
for a lumberyard.

20:00.742 --> 20:01.826
Really?
That's great!

20:01.951 --> 20:03.328
You mean,
you don't mind?

20:03.453 --> 20:05.205
No, I hate
the rainforest.

20:05.330 --> 20:07.874
You go right ahead and plow down
this whole fucking thing.

20:07.999 --> 20:08.917
That's swell!

20:09.042 --> 20:10.835
Okay, Lenny, so,

20:10.960 --> 20:12.128
in order for our long-distance
relationship to work,

20:12.253 --> 20:13.421
we'll have to call each other
every other day.

20:13.546 --> 20:14.464
Mrph rmhmhm rm.

20:14.589 --> 20:16.799
Aah!

20:16.925 --> 20:19.260
Aah! Lenny, no!

20:19.385 --> 20:21.012
Oh, my God!
They killed Kenny!

20:21.137 --> 20:22.388
You bastards!

20:22.513 --> 20:24.766
What?! Who?!
Who killed him?!

20:25.683 --> 20:26.601
They did.

20:26.726 --> 20:27.644
Who's "they"?

20:27.769 --> 20:29.896
You know, "they".

20:30.021 --> 20:31.856
They're--
they're bastards.

20:31.981 --> 20:33.441
Well, don't just stand there!
Help him!

20:33.566 --> 20:35.109
What?
Help... him?

20:35.235 --> 20:36.611
Ugh!

20:36.736 --> 20:38.780
Come on, Benny!
Breathe!

20:40.448 --> 20:42.992
Breathe,
you son of a bitch!

20:44.744 --> 20:45.954
[coughs]

20:46.829 --> 20:47.664
Whoa, dude!

20:47.789 --> 20:50.083
And now,

20:50.208 --> 20:52.252
here to teach us
about the rainforest

20:52.377 --> 20:54.212
is "Getting Gay With Kids."

20:54.337 --> 20:56.839
Does everybody remember
the new lyrics?

20:56.965 --> 20:59.425
And...
♪ Doo-doo-dee-doo ♪

20:59.550 --> 21:01.219
♪ Zada-doo-dee-wow ♪

21:01.344 --> 21:02.679
Boys: ♪ There's a place
called the rainforest ♪

21:02.804 --> 21:04.514
♪ That truly sucks ass ♪

21:04.639 --> 21:07.767
All: ♪ Let's knock it all down
and get rid of it fast ♪

21:07.892 --> 21:09.310
Boys: ♪ You say,
"save the rainforest" ♪

21:09.435 --> 21:11.312
♪ But what do you know? ♪

21:11.437 --> 21:16.025
All: ♪ You've never been
to the rainforest before ♪

21:16.150 --> 21:19.279
♪ Getting Gay With Kids
is here ♪

21:19.404 --> 21:22.782
♪ To tell you things
you might not like to hear ♪

21:22.907 --> 21:26.035
♪ You only fight these causes
'cause caring sells ♪

21:26.160 --> 21:29.414
♪ All you activists can go
fuck yourselves ♪

21:29.539 --> 21:30.707
That was so inspiring.

21:30.832 --> 21:32.041
What a wonderful
message.

21:32.166 --> 21:34.711
Boy: ♪...Boys and girls ♪

21:34.836 --> 21:38.006
Kelly: ♪ There'll be no more
rainforests ♪

21:38.131 --> 21:40.550
♪ Left in
the entire world ♪

21:40.675 --> 21:41.551
♪ World ♪

21:41.676 --> 21:43.094
♪ World ♪

21:43.219 --> 21:45.555
♪ Getting Gay With Kids
is here ♪

21:45.680 --> 21:49.058
♪ To spread the word
and bring you cheer ♪

21:49.183 --> 21:52.228
♪ Getting Gay With Kids
is here ♪

21:52.353 --> 21:54.063
♪ Let's knock down
the rainforest ♪

21:54.188 --> 21:56.065
♪ What do you say? ♪

21:56.190 --> 21:58.359
♪ It's totally gay ♪

21:58.484 --> 21:59.444
♪ It's totally gay ♪
